===Talk to Luka and start his "trial"{{subst:void|<!--201160107-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Boulder Town|update|It's still a new experience for you to watch Luka defend his title. However, it is just another ordinary day for Luka.<br />Luka tells you and Seele about his "trial plans" and wants you to accompany him the whole way to witness his improvement.<br />As someone who doesn't know how to say no, of course you agree to his request.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
----
;(Screen fades to black)
:'''Natasha:''' Luka... can you hear me?
:'''Luka:''' ...
:'''Seele:''' Hey... Hey! Luka, you're up!
:'''Luka:''' Ugh... I...
----
:'''Seele:''' Ha, you're finally awake! You've been out for the whole day. We were really worried!
:'''Natasha:''' Don't worry, Seele. Like I said, it was just the exhaustion. Svarog was deliberately holding back.
:<!--1.5-second delay-->
:'''Luka:''' Seele... (Trailblazer)... and... Nat? I'm in... the clinic?
:'''Seele:''' ...Where else? You think we'd leave you on Svarog's turf?
;(Return to previous option selection)
:'''Luka:''' Ha... thank you all. I feel much better now. Sorry, Nat... I must have wasted your time.
:'''Natasha:''' Don't be ridiculous, Luka. Still, whatever your motivation was, I hope you can find a different outlet for it.
:'''Seele:''' ...I'm not gonna let you off the hook that easy &mdash; there's more to this story. You need to explain what the heck got into you today.
;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Svarog hit pretty hard.
::'''Seele:''' Like I said, he's a robot... No matter how good his calculations are, he's not designed to pull punches.
::'''Luka:''' Hahaha... you're always so serious. I've said it before &mdash; this is my train&mdash; *coughing*
::'''Natasha:''' ...Slow down &mdash; you haven't completely recovered. Seele, don't pressure him... let him rest.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That victory slogan of yours...
::'''Seele:''' The one good thing about you losing is that we didn't have to hear it again.
::'''Luka:''' Hahaha... you're always so serious. I've said it before &mdash; this is my train&mdash; *coughing*
::'''Natasha:''' ...Slow down &mdash; you haven't completely recovered. Seele, don't pressure him... let him rest.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why did you insist on fighting Svarog?
::'''Seele:''' That's on me too... I should've refused him straightaway. I had a bad feeling from the start.
::'''Luka:''' Hahaha... you're always so serious. I've said it before &mdash; this is my train&mdash; *coughing*
::'''Natasha:''' ...Slow down &mdash; you haven't completely recovered. Seele, don't pressure him... let him rest.
:;(Return to previous option selection)

;(Talk to Natasha)
:'''Natasha:''' Please go ask Oleg about this, (Trailblazer)
:'''Natasha:''' Don't let small things get in the way of your friendship.
{{Dialogue End}}

===Talk to Oleg and ask about Luka{{subst:void|<!--201160109-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Boulder Town|update|Luka fought until he passed out in his battle with Svarog. He still refuses to tell you and Seele the true purpose behind his "trial" even after he woke up.<br />You decide to ask Oleg, his trainer, whether Luka's been acting weird recently.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Oleg)
;(First interaction)
::'''Oleg:''' Yo, we meet again, (Trailblazer)! I thought you all left to save the world or something already.
::'''Oleg:''' Good timing, I still owe you a thank you: Thanks for getting this city back on the right track, outsider.
::'''Oleg:''' Before this place is completely handed over to the Silvermane Guards, Wildfire still has to oversee the Underworld's daily affairs. Feel free to speak up if you need anything.
;(Subsequent interactions)
::'''Oleg:''' Hey, we meet again, (Trailblazer)!
::'''Oleg:''' As long as you're in the Underworld, Wildfire will always treat you with utmost hospitality. Never hesitate to speak your needs.
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} Let's have a "Hyperlink Match"!
::'''Oleg:''' Challenge me? Alright, but I'm not very good, go easy on me, okay?
:<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.ShowUI",
	"Name": "Ui.AetherDivide.AetherChallenge.AetherChallengePage",
	"WaitForExit": true,
	"Param": {
		"Value": "4"
	}
}</pre>
;(If {{Mission|Future Market (II)|showChapter=0}} has been completed)
:{{Диалог}} That agreement was not signed.
::'''Oleg:''' Miss Bronya made a bold decision and I respect her for it, even though it was not exactly what I believed best.
::'''Oleg:''' I imagine she must have found a better solution, right?
::'''Oleg:''' There is actually someone in the IPC who shares the same ideals as Miss Bronya...
::'''Oleg:''' Although it is hard to believe, resolving this situation with peaceful methods is the best-case scenario.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} About the clash in the Great Mine...
::'''Oleg:''' You think the mine workers will be looking for trouble with the IPC? Don't worry. We've already resolved this.
::'''Oleg:''' Those people dressed in black came to visit the Underworld later and promised that they will pay for their improper actions from before. All of the miners will be receiving a considerable sum.
::'''Oleg:''' Though this repayment will not be made immediately, it shows the IPC's meticulous style of handling affairs. Perhaps they will genuinely become great partners.
::'''Oleg:''' As for how far this cooperation will go, we will need to see what methods are used on both sides. I hope that Miss Bronya can handle this heavy responsibility.
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} I wanna ask you some things about Luka.
::----
::'''Oleg:''' ...Oh? My student? Did something happen recently?
::'''Oleg:''' I was wondering why he didn't come and see me after the championship match ended. Come, tell me about it.
::{{Black Screen|You tell Oleg about everything that happened with Luka and Seele...}}
::'''Oleg:''' Mm... that does sound a little strange. Luka usually doesn't push himself so far...
::'''Oleg:''' ...Huh, he may be a tough guy on the surface, but he's got his secrets. Did he tell you about the origins of his mechanical arm?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} He mentioned something before he fought Svarog.
:::'''Oleg:''' Ah, then he probably didn't describe the scene in detail.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't remember.
:::'''Oleg:''' Well, let me tell you about it.
::'''Oleg:''' That was... six? Seven years ago? I was patrolling with some comrades in the neighboring town of Moltammerville &mdash; we passed an ordinary mechanics shop.
::'''Oleg:''' There was a serious-looking fella looking after the shop. He was probably a few years younger than me, but his hair and beard were white as snow. There was a young lad doing odd jobs &mdash; he looked pretty exhausted.
::'''Oleg:''' Anyway, I convinced the shopkeeper to let him come with me.
::'''Oleg:''' Luka was a fast learner. At first, I couldn't figure out if he liked what I was teaching him &mdash; fighting, weapons, strategy, etc. He didn't talk a lot &mdash; just kept his head down.
::'''Oleg:''' Then... about a year after I took him in, Luka lost one of his arms while rescuing townsfolk from the Fragmentum in Moltammerville.
::'''Oleg:''' ...He almost didn't make it &mdash; he was unconscious for two or three days. I sat next to his bed, anxious and guilty. Guess what he said to me after he woke up?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...Go on.
::'''Oleg:''' "Master, I feel great!"
::'''Oleg:''' He had bandages all over his body &mdash; most of his wounds hadn't healed yet... But, it was the first time he'd ever smiled at me. I still remember that expression.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And the moral of the story is...?
:::'''Oleg:''' Oh, sorry, I get a little carried away when I tell this story, hahaha.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Guess that kind of sums him up, huh...
:::'''Oleg:''' Can't tell from looking at him, right?
::'''Oleg:''' What I'm trying to say is: Luka views other people's lives as more important than his own. That's how he's always been.
::'''Oleg:''' So when he says stuff like "this is for training" &mdash; that's probably a lie. He's hiding something from you alright.
::'''Oleg:''' Anyway, I'm too old to be getting involved in this stuff. I'm sure you and Seele can sort this by yourselves.
::'''Oleg:''' One thing I will ask &mdash; please try not to embarrass him too much, okay? He's the fighting champion of Boulder Town, after all &mdash; an idol for all the children. He needs to keep up that image, haha.
::----
;(If {{Mission|Future Market (II)|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог}} What happened at the Corridor of Fading Echoes?
::'''Oleg:''' Oh, you're still thinking about that? What a kindhearted person, hahaha.
::'''Oleg:''' Honestly, nothing much has changed. Every time we clear out one swarm, more monsters just pour out of the Fragmentum.
::'''Oleg:''' But we cannot give up. As long as there's a tomorrow, we will continue with our fight.
::'''Oleg:''' "Tomorrow" &mdash; now that's a luxury that you've won for us, (Trailblazer). We certainly won't squander it.
;(If {{Mission|Future Market (II)|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог}} Let's talk, Oleg.
::'''Oleg:''' Oh? You've really come to just chat with me? Hahaha, fire away! I like talking to young people.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What have you been up to recently?
:::'''Oleg:''' Helping Natasha calm any Underworld unrest, performing post-disaster rebuilding work &mdash; she's the brains of the outfit, and I'm the brawn. Not much difference from usual, but I'm much happier and relaxed.
:::'''Oleg:''' Also, many younger people around me have been taking this chance to leave Boulder Town to try their luck in the Overworld. I've chatted plenty with them, to give them some of life's pointers, I guess.
:::'''Oleg:''' You know young 'uns, it helps that they are brimming with passion. Who knows when they'll make it someday in the Overworld? At least they won't reminisce and be filled with regret.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Were you part of the Silvermane Guards?
:::'''Oleg:''' Yes, you've heard?
:::'''Oleg:''' Those were the glory days... I don't mean to brag, but in the prime of my youth, everyone knew of my repute as "Swiftstrike Oleg."
:::'''Oleg:''' ...No point waxing lyrical about the past though. One shouldn't be stuck in the past at my age. We should embrace the present and seize the day. Hahaha!
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Wildfire's future...
:::'''Oleg:''' Realistically speaking, (Trailblazer), Wildfire will be disbanded eventually. Natasha and I have been aware of this since the day we established it.
:::'''Oleg:''' A healthy, normal Underworld doesn't need an existence like Wildfire's. Don't worry though, even if we do disband, there'll be plenty of youngsters who will carry on the will of Wildfire.
:::'''Oleg:''' Seele and my rowdy apprentice, they will keep fighting for their home. So long as their aspirations never change, I have nothing but high hopes for the Underworld's future. Hahaha!
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Bronya is the Supreme Guardian now.
:::'''Oleg:''' Oh, that girl... I knew she was special the first time I laid eyes on her.
:::'''Oleg:''' To a certain extent, I feel like she's just like when Cocolia was younger, and trust me, that's definitely a compliment. Except that Bronya's less glum, and more sincere.
:::'''Oleg:''' I believe she will restore Belobog to when it was before the blockade, or perhaps even better. I mean, you all already took care of that Stellaron thing, didn't you?
:::'''Oleg:''' A major undertaking can't be accomplished by a single person, regardless of her individual strength. It's a good thing her sincerity has touched so many, and we're all glad to be helping her.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} Nice chat.
:::'''Oleg:''' Oh, leaving already? I haven't had my fill, hahaha!
;(If {{Mission|Future Market (II)|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} Goodbye, Oleg.
::'''Oleg:''' Go well, young one. Do what you all need to do. I hope we will meet again in the coming days.
